.TH SW-PYDOCS 1 "September 2026" "SignalWire SDK" "SignalWire Commands"
.SH NAME
sw-pydocs \- print the SignalWire SDK's documentation for the installed version
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sw-pydocs
.br
.B sw-pydocs
.I topic
.RI [ name ]
.br
.B sw-pydocs
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sw-pydocs
prints the documentation that ships with the signalwire-sdk package, as
Markdown, for people and for coding agents. With no arguments it prints an
index: what the SDK does, where to start, and every topic. Each topic
describes an area and lists the installed docs to read, examples and API
names, with full paths.
.PP
Facts come from the installed package, so they match the installed version:
the commands, the built-in skills and their parameters, the REST namespaces,
the environment variables the code reads, and every signature and docstring.
.PP
.B python -m signalwire
runs the same command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I topic \fR[\fIname\fR]
Print a topic, such as agents, tools, contexts, skills, relay, rest, search or
deploy.
.B sw-pydocs topics
lists them all. The skills topic takes a skill name and prints its parameters.
.TP
.BI "api " name
Print the signature, docstring, source location and members of an SDK name,
such as AgentBase, FunctionResult.connect or signalwire.relay.Call.
.TP
.BR examples " [\fIfilter\fR]"
List the installed examples with descriptions and paths: all of them, those
for a topic, or those matching a word.
.TP
.BI "grep " regex
Search the installed docs and examples, ignoring case.
.B \-\-code
also searches the SDK's source, and
.BI \-\-limit " n"
sets the most lines printed (default 100).
.TP
.BI "show " file
Print an installed doc, named by path, file name or stem.
.B \-\-toc
lists its headings, and
.BI \-\-section " heading"
prints the first section whose heading contains the text.
.TP
.BR path " [\fIfile\fR]"
Print the directory the docs are installed in, or one file's full path.
.TP
.B init
Add a section about
.B sw-pydocs
to the AGENTS.md in the current directory, or in
.BI \-\-dir " directory" \fR.
.B \-\-skill
also writes an Agent Skills SKILL.md, and
.B \-\-print
prints the section without writing it.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed SDK version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when a name or file isn't found, and 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaig-test (1),
.BR sw-search (1),
.BR sw-agent-init (1)
